melody:
# Verse (as published by Leo Feist, 1917)
John-nie get your gun, get your gun, get your gun,
Bb4/ C5/ D5/ Bb4/ G4 G4/ F4/ G4 G4/ F4/ G4(2)
Take it on the run, on the run, on the run;
C5/ D5/ Eb5/ C5/ G4 G4/ F#4/ G4 G4/ F#4/ G4(2)
Hear them call-ing you and me, Ev-'ry son of lib-er-ty.
G#4 A4 D5 C5 A4 Bb4 D5(2) C5 A4 C5 D5 A4 G4 C5(2)
Hur-ry right a-way, no de-lay, go to-day,
Bb4/ C5/ D5/ Bb4/ G4 G4/ F4/ G4 G4/ F4/ G4(2)
Make your dad-dy glad to have had such a lad.
C5/ D5/ Eb5/ C5/ G4 G4/ F#4/ G4 G4/ F#4/ G4(2)
Tell your sweet-heart not to pine, To be proud her boy's in line.
G#4 A4 D5 C5 A4 Bb4 D5 A4/ Bb4/ C5 C5 C5 C5 C5(2) ~C5/ r/

# Chorus
O-ver there, o-ver there, Send the word, send the word o-ver there
D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/ D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/ D5/ F4/ Bb4 D5/ F4/ Bb4 D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/
That the Yanks are com-ing, the Yanks are com-ing, The drums rum-tum-ming ev-'ry-where.
C5/ D5/ Eb5 D5 C5/ F5 Eb5/ D5 C5 Bb4/ D5 Bb4/ A4 C5 Bb4/ A4/ Bb4/ G4/ C5(2) ~C5/ r/
So pre-pare, say a pray'r, Send the word, send the word to be-ware.
D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/ D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/ D5/ F4/ Bb4 D5/ F4/ Bb4 D5/ F4/ Bb4(2) ~Bb4/ r/
We'll be o-ver, we're com-ing o-ver, And we won't come back till it's o-ver, o-ver there!
D5/ C5/ Bb4(2) F4/ D5/ C5/ Bb4/ C5(2) F4 G4/ A4/ Bb4 Bb4 Bb4 Bb4/ Bb4/ Bb4/ A4/ G4/ A4/ Bb4

